Original commit body from c6eea50:

Documents the systematic gap where only 5 of 67 analyzers track imports
for call resolution disambiguation, despite investing in the shared
SymbolResolver framework that supports path_hint.

Key findings:
- Phase 1: JS/TS and Kotlin have bugs (imports tracked but not used)
- Phase 2: 8 high-value languages should add tracking
- Phase 3A: 20 more languages where tracking matters (triaged by
  whether aliased/qualified imports are idiomatic)
- Phase 3B: 17 languages where tracking doesn't help (dynamic/textual)
- Category C: 17 config/data formats (N/A)

This ADR was prompted by PR #503 which fixed Python's submodule import
resolution. The investigation revealed the broader pattern.

References: ADR-0006 (type inference), commits afc727a-d8f936d
(resolution framework rollout)
